{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"Voltius.Voltius","latestVersion":"0.68.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Cross-platform SSH client and terminal","license":"AGPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/VoltiusApp/voltius/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Cross-platform SSH client and terminal","license":"AGPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/VoltiusApp/voltius/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","moniker":"voltius","name":"Voltius","packageUrl":"https://voltius.app/","publisher":"Voltius","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/VoltiusApp/voltius/issues","publisherUrl":"https://voltius.app/","releaseNotes":"Added\n- On macOS, Voltius reads a configuration profile pushed by an MDM (Jamf, Intune, Kandji, Mosyle) as machine policy, with the same keys as Android and iOS: policy, server_url, server_allow_other and enrollment_token. Only device profiles count. Where the profile and policy.json both set a key, the profile wins, and voltius-cli policy check warns about the overlap. The Free plan row now reads \"Managed configuration (MDM)\" (#842)\n- On a machine enrolled through its machine policy, the enrolling team's policy now applies whichever account is active: signed out, offline accounts, accounts on other servers and accounts outside the team. Voltius keeps it on the device, so it also applies at startup without a connection. Rotate and Revoke in the Members share sheet now say what happens to enrolled devices (#845)\nFixed\n- On macOS, Ctrl key combinations now reach the terminal (Ctrl+C, D, Z, R, L, V, K, F, …). App shortcuts moved to Cmd: Cmd+C / Cmd+V copy and paste in the terminal, Cmd+K opens the palette, Cmd+W closes a tab, and Settings shows them as Cmd. Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Space and Ctrl+Option+D stay on Ctrl because macOS uses the Cmd versions. On Linux and Windows, holding the Super/Windows key no longer triggers a Ctrl shortcut (#843)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/VoltiusApp/voltius/releases/tag/v0.68.0","tags":["crdt","credential-manager","homelab","local-first","plugins","port-forwarding","rust","serial","sftp","ssh","ssh-client","sync","sysadmin","tauri","teams","terminal"]}},"moniker":"voltius","name":"Voltius","packageUrl":"https://voltius.app/","publisher":"Voltius","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/VoltiusApp/voltius/issues","publisherUrl":"https://voltius.app/","releaseNotes":"Added\n- On macOS, Voltius reads a configuration profile pushed by an MDM (Jamf, Intune, Kandji, Mosyle) as machine policy, with the same keys as Android and iOS: policy, server_url, server_allow_other and enrollment_token. Only device profiles count. Where the profile and policy.json both set a key, the profile wins, and voltius-cli policy check warns about the overlap. The Free plan row now reads \"Managed configuration (MDM)\" (#842)\n- On a machine enrolled through its machine policy, the enrolling team's policy now applies whichever account is active: signed out, offline accounts, accounts on other servers and accounts outside the team. Voltius keeps it on the device, so it also applies at startup without a connection. Rotate and Revoke in the Members share sheet now say what happens to enrolled devices (#845)\nFixed\n- On macOS, Ctrl key combinations now reach the terminal (Ctrl+C, D, Z, R, L, V, K, F, …). App shortcuts moved to Cmd: Cmd+C / Cmd+V copy and paste in the terminal, Cmd+K opens the palette, Cmd+W closes a tab, and Settings shows them as Cmd. Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Space and Ctrl+Option+D stay on Ctrl because macOS uses the Cmd versions. On Linux and Windows, holding the Super/Windows key no longer triggers a Ctrl shortcut (#843)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/VoltiusApp/voltius/releases/tag/v0.68.0","tags":["crdt","credential-manager","homelab","local-first","plugins","port-forwarding","rust","serial","sftp","ssh","ssh-client","sync","sysadmin","tauri","teams","terminal"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions